# Line-ending policy. Committing this does NOT rewrite existing files -- the
# tree is currently mixed (mostly CRLF, some LF). A dedicated normalization
# commit (`git add --renormalize .`) should follow, on its own, so its large
# whitespace-only diff never mixes with a logic change.
#
# After renormalization: text files are LF in the repo, checked out native on
# each platform, so a Linux checkout gets working `#!` shebangs (CRLF shebangs
# fail to exec) and Windows still sees CRLF in the editor.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Explicit text types (belt and suspenders; text=auto covers most)
*.py    text eol=lf
*.md    text eol=lf
*.toml  text eol=lf
*.cfg   text eol=lf
*.txt   text eol=lf
*.json  text eol=lf
*.csv   text eol=lf
*.yml   text eol=lf
*.yaml  text eol=lf
*.sigmf-meta text eol=lf

# Binary: never touched, never diffed as text
*.iq            binary
*.sigmf-data    binary
*.wav           binary
*.npy           binary
*.png           binary
*.svg           text eol=lf
